      "id": "SDN-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "One scaled trace-dual basis for all residue maps",
      "anchor": "inputs-split-denominator",
      "statement": "For finite Galois F/L′, some nonzero b₀∈𝒪_L′ works simultaneously for every finite field k and every r:𝒪_F→k with surjective base restriction r₀ and r₀(b₀)≠0. The conjugate reductions induce 𝒪_F/(ker r₀)𝒪_F≃∏_(σ∈Gal(F/L′))k.",
      "hypotheses": "Number fields with F/L′ finite Galois. Field trace is taken down to L′. Both the basis and its trace dual are cleared by one integer. The displayed isomorphism restates the surjectivity and kernel clauses of Split.",
      "definitions": [
        "trace-dual basis",
        "linear independence of automorphisms",
        "extended ideal",
        "residue field"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-split-trace",
        "inputs-split-residue-ring"
      ],
