    {
      "id": "SDN-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Enlarging the denominator to include the divisor support",
      "anchor": "inputs-split-support",
      "statement": "For a finite divisor 𝔡 the choice B=b₀∏Norm(P) over its support is nonzero, divisible by b₀ and belongs to every prime in that support. A map between two corresponding finite-coordinate lattices preserves their common localization after inverting B. Conjugate residue tuples therefore apply at all admissible tests away from B.",
      "hypotheses": "Finite support, integral B, finitely many coordinates. Powers of B clearing a vector may depend on that vector. For the split tests require r₀ onto and r₀(B)≠0.",
      "definitions": [
        "divisor support",
        "localized lattice",
        "integral gluing map"
      ],
